Reachable Web Observatory source-code rights notice
Effective: 2026-07-26

Reachable Web Observatory includes a Go reimplementation and extension of the
private Python system behind What's on HTTP, created by elixx. Publication of
the Go reimplementation was authorized by elixx, but that authorization did not
specify an open-source license.

This repository previously displayed a blanket MIT notice before authority to
offer portions based on the original system under MIT had been documented. That
notice should not be relied upon as a verified statement of rights for those
portions.

No new license to use, copy, modify, or redistribute the source code is offered
by this repository while downstream licensing is clarified.

This source-code notice does not change the separate CC-BY-4.0 license for
independently collected Observatory metadata and applicable database rights.
See LICENSE-DATA, LICENSING.md, and PROVENANCE.md.
